// Print a string using nextline
The nextLine() method in Java is a function of the java.util.Scanner class. It reads a full line of text from an input stream (like standard input/keyboard or a file) up until a newline character (\n) or Enter key press

Reading Full Phrases or Sentences: Unlike next(), which stops reading at the first space, nextLine() preserves spaces and reads the entire line of text as a single String

CODE:

import java.util.Scanner;
public class Main{
    public static void main(String []args){
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter your string:");
        String str = input.nextLine();
        System.out.println("Value:"+str);
    }
}
